{"metadata":{"kernelspec":{"display_name":"Python 3","language":"python","name":"python3"},"language_info":{"name":"python","version":"3.13.16","mimetype":"text/x-python","codemirror_mode":{"name":"ipython","version":3},"pygments_lexer":"ipython3","nbconvert_exporter":"python","file_extension":".py"},"kaggle":{"accelerator":"nvidiaTeslaT4","dataSources":[{"sourceType":"datasetVersion","sourceId":22675563}],"dockerImageVersionId":31523,"isInternetEnabled":true,"language":"python","sourceType":"notebook","isGpuEnabled":false}},"nbformat_minor":4,"nbformat":4,"cells":[{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"# RAG Pipeline with a Vector Database (ChromaDB)\n**AIML506 · Department of Computer Science and Engineering · East West University . Fall 2026**  \n\n### Project: GridTrace — An Explainable Smart-Grid Transaction Investigation Assistant\n* **Dataset:** *Smart Grid Blockchain Transaction Dataset* (Mendeley Data DOI: [10.17632/w59j6hyc25.1](https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/w59j6hyc25/1), CC BY 4.0)\n* **Vector Database:** ChromaDB (Persisted to `/kaggle/working/chroma_db`)\n* **Embedding Model:** `sentence-transformers/all-MiniLM-L6-v2` (Dense cosine embeddings)\n* **Primary Generator:** `Qwen3-4B-Instruct-2507` (4-bit NF4 quantized via `bitsandbytes` on GPU)\n* **Model Ablation:** `Qwen3-8B` (Tested under identical context budget, prompt, and benchmark questions)\n\n`CSV Records → Cleaning & Serialization → Document Chunks → ChromaDB (HNSW Cosine) → Top-k Dense Retrieval → Qwen3-4B / Qwen3-8B → Cited JSON Claims`\n\n---\n### Setup Instructions for Kaggle\n1. **Accelerator:** Under **Notebook Options** (right pane), set **Accelerator** to **GPU T4** or **GPU T4 x 2**.\n2. **Internet:** Set **Internet** to **On** (required for pip packages and downloading Hugging Face model weights).\n3. **Dataset:** Attach the dataset `Smart Grid Blockchain Transaction Dataset` via **Add Input -> Datasets** or upload `blockchain_transactions.csv`.\n","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"## Background: Variations of Vector-Database RAG\nFollowing the taxonomy of Gao et al. (2023), RAG systems are grouped into three paradigms:\n\n| Stage | Core Idea | Pipeline |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Naive RAG** | Index once, retrieve top-$k$ by similarity, generate answer | `chunk → embed → top-k → generate` |\n| **Advanced RAG** | Pre-retrieval query expansion, hybrid search, cross-encoder reranking | `rewrite → retrieve → rerank → generate` |\n| **Modular / Agentic RAG** | Dynamic routing, multi-hop sub-query decomposition, self-critique | `plan → retrieve → verify → generate` |\n\nThis notebook implements an **Advanced Naive RAG** baseline with:\n1. **Relational Document Serialization:** Structuring tabular blockchain rows into coherent natural-language documents with rich metadata.\n2. **HNSW Cosine Indexing:** Fast approximate nearest neighbor search via ChromaDB.\n3. **Strict Citation Validation:** Rejecting any hallucinated claims whose citations do not match retrieved source IDs.\n4. **Unified Pipeline Alignment:** Using the exact same generator model, prompt template, context budget, and benchmark questions as the companion GraphRAG notebook.\n","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"%pip install -q chromadb sentence-transformers transformers accelerate bitsandbytes\n","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-24T14:17:58.495108Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-24T14:17:58.496004Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-24T14:18:19.622119Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-11-24T14:17:58.49595Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-24T14:18:19.621286Z"}},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","text":"\u001b[31mERROR: pip's dependency resolver does not currently take into account all the packages that are installed. This behaviour is the source of the following dependency conflicts.\ntweepy 4.17.0 requires oauthlib<4,>=3.2.0, but you have oauthlib 4.0.1 which is incompatible.\ngradio 6.30.0 requires pillow<13.0,>=8.0, but you have pillow 13.0.0 which is incompatible.\ngoogle-adk 2.7.1 requires opentelemetry-api<=1.42.1,>=1.39, but you have opentelemetry-api 1.45.2 which is incompatible.\ngoogle-adk 2.7.1 requires opentelemetry-sdk<=1.42.1,>=1.39, but you have opentelemetry-sdk 1.45.2 which is incompatible.\u001b[0m\u001b[31m\n\u001b[0mNote: you may need to restart the kernel to use updated packages.\n","output_type":"stream"}],"execution_count":1},{"cell_type":"code","source":"import atexit\nimport gc\nimport json\nimport os\nimport re\nimport sys\nimport time\nimport csv\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfrom collections import Counter, defaultdict\n\nimport chromadb\nfrom chromadb.utils import embedding_functions\nimport torch\nfrom transformers import AutoTokenizer, AutoModelForCausalLM, BitsAndBytesConfig\n\nprint(f\"Python: {sys.version.split()[0]} | PyTorch: {torch.__version__} | ChromaDB: {chromadb.__version__}\")\nprint(f\"CUDA Available: {torch.cuda.is_available()}\")\nif torch.cuda.is_available():\n    print(f\"GPU Accelerator: {torch.cuda.get_device_name(0)}\")\n\n# Unified Configuration\nPRIMARY_MODEL_ID = \"Qwen/Qwen3-4B-Instruct-2507\"\nABLATION_MODEL_ID = \"Qwen/Qwen3-8B\"\nFALLBACK_4B_ID = \"Qwen/Qwen2.5-3B-Instruct\"     # Fallback if 4B checkpoint is gated/offline\nFALLBACK_8B_ID = \"Qwen/Qwen2.5-7B-Instruct\"     # Fallback for ablation\nEMBEDDING_MODEL_NAME = \"all-MiniLM-L6-v2\"\nCHROMA_PATH = \"/kaggle/working/chroma_db\"\nCOLLECTION_NAME = \"gridtrace_vectorrag\"\nTOP_K_BUDGET = 5\n","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-24T14:18:19.623957Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-24T14:18:19.624337Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-24T14:18:47.055517Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-11-24T14:18:19.624312Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-24T14:18:47.054827Z"}},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","text":"Python: 3.13.16 | PyTorch: 2.11.0+cu130 | ChromaDB: 1.5.9\nCUDA Available: True\nGPU Accelerator: Tesla T4\n","output_type":"stream"}],"execution_count":2},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"## 1. Load and Inspect the Smart Grid Dataset\nWe locate `blockchain_transactions.csv` within `/kaggle/input` or the local directory, validating row counts, the genesis block, and participant types.\n","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"def locate_dataset():\n    candidates = [\n        Path(\"/kaggle/input\"),\n        Path(\"./Smart Grid Blockchain Transaction Dataset\"),\n        Path(\".\")\n    ]\n    for d in candidates:\n        if d.exists():\n            matches = list(d.rglob(\"blockchain_transactions.csv\"))\n            if matches:\n                return matches[0]\n    raise FileNotFoundError(\"blockchain_transactions.csv not found. Attach dataset to Kaggle.\")\n\ndataset_csv = locate_dataset()\nprint(f\"Loaded dataset from: {dataset_csv} ({dataset_csv.stat().st_size / (1024*1024):.2f} MB)\")\n\nwith open(dataset_csv, mode=\"r\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n    raw_rows = list(csv.DictReader(f))\n\nprint(f\"Total raw records : {len(raw_rows):,}\")\n\n# Separate genesis block and transaction records\ntransaction_rows = [r for r in raw_rows if r[\"tx_id\"].strip()]\nblocks_set = set(int(r[\"block_index\"]) for r in raw_rows)\nparticipants_set = set(r[\"tx_sender\"] for r in transaction_rows) | set(r[\"tx_recipient\"] for r in transaction_rows)\ntx_types = Counter(r[\"tx_type\"] for r in transaction_rows)\n\nprint(f\"Non-genesis Transactions : {len(transaction_rows):,}\")\nprint(f\"Distinct Blocks          : {len(blocks_set):,} (Blocks 0 to {max(blocks_set)})\")\nprint(f\"Distinct Participants    : {len(participants_set):,} ({len([p for p in participants_set if p.startswith('CON')])} Consumers, {len([p for p in participants_set if p.startswith('PRO')])} Prosumers, 1 Miner/Operator)\")\nprint(f\"Transaction Breakdown    : {dict(tx_types)}\")\n","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-24T14:18:47.056636Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-24T14:18:47.057225Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-24T14:18:47.339833Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-11-24T14:18:47.057199Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-24T14:18:47.339019Z"}},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","text":"Loaded dataset from: /kaggle/input/datasets/suchonabiswas27/blockchain-transaction-dataset/blockchain_transactions.csv (2.74 MB)\nTotal raw records : 10,206\nNon-genesis Transactions : 10,205\nDistinct Blocks          : 490 (Blocks 0 to 489)\nDistinct Participants    : 31 (20 Consumers, 10 Prosumers, 1 Miner/Operator)\nTransaction Breakdown    : {'energy_delivery': 5193, 'energy_payment': 5012}\n","output_type":"stream"}],"execution_count":3},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"## 2. Document Serialization & Metadata Indexing\nTo allow semantic embedding of relational records, each transaction and each block header is serialized into an information-dense text document with explicit metadata fields for filtering.\n","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"def serialize_transaction(r):\n    energy_val = float(r.get(\"tx_energy\", 0.0))\n\n    return (\n        f\"Smart Grid Transaction Record:\\n\"\n        f\"Transaction ID: {r['tx_id']}\\n\"\n        f\"Transaction Type: {r['tx_type']}\\n\"\n        f\"Sender: {r['tx_sender']}\\n\"\n        f\"Recipient: {r['tx_recipient']}\\n\"\n        f\"Amount: {float(r['tx_amount']):.6f}\\n\"\n        f\"Energy: {energy_val:.6f}\\n\"\n        f\"Timestamp: {r['tx_timestamp']}\\n\"\n        f\"Block Index: {r['block_index']}\\n\"\n        f\"Block Hash: {r['block_hash']}\\n\"\n        f\"Previous Block Hash: {r['block_previous_hash']}\"\n    )\n\ndef extract_block_records(rows):\n    blocks_dict = {}\n    for r in rows:\n        b_idx = int(r[\"block_index\"])\n        if b_idx not in blocks_dict:\n            blocks_dict[b_idx] = {\n                \"block_index\": b_idx,\n                \"block_timestamp\": r[\"block_timestamp\"],\n                \"block_miner_id\": r[\"block_miner_id\"],\n                \"block_hash\": r[\"block_hash\"],\n                \"block_previous_hash\": r[\"block_previous_hash\"],\n                \"block_nonce\": r[\"block_nonce\"],\n                \"tx_count\": 0\n            }\n        if r[\"tx_id\"].strip():\n            blocks_dict[b_idx][\"tx_count\"] += 1\n    return blocks_dict\n\nblocks_dict = extract_block_records(raw_rows)\n\ndef serialize_block(b):\n    return (\n        f\"Smart Grid Block Header Record:\\n\"\n        f\"Block Index: {b['block_index']}\\n\"\n        f\"Recorded Miner: {b['block_miner_id']}\\n\"\n        f\"Transactions Included: {b['tx_count']}\\n\"\n        f\"Block Hash: {b['block_hash']}\\n\"\n        f\"Previous Block Hash: {b['block_previous_hash']}\\n\"\n        f\"Nonce: {b['block_nonce']}\\n\"\n        f\"Block Timestamp: {b['block_timestamp']}\"\n    )\n\n# Prepare documents for ChromaDB\ncorpus_documents, corpus_ids, corpus_metadatas = [], [], []\n\nfor r in transaction_rows:\n    corpus_documents.append(serialize_transaction(r))\n    corpus_ids.append(f\"tx-{r['tx_id']}\")\n    corpus_metadatas.append({\n        \"doc_type\": \"transaction\",\n        \"tx_id\": r[\"tx_id\"],\n        \"tx_type\": r[\"tx_type\"],\n        \"sender\": r[\"tx_sender\"],\n        \"recipient\": r[\"tx_recipient\"],\n        \"block_index\": int(r[\"block_index\"]),\n        \"amount\": float(r[\"tx_amount\"])\n    })\n\nfor b_idx in sorted(blocks_dict.keys()):\n    b = blocks_dict[b_idx]\n    corpus_documents.append(serialize_block(b))\n    corpus_ids.append(f\"block-{b_idx}\")\n    corpus_metadatas.append({\n        \"doc_type\": \"block\",\n        \"tx_id\": \"\",\n        \"tx_type\": \"block_header\",\n        \"sender\": b[\"block_miner_id\"],\n        \"recipient\": \"\",\n        \"block_index\": b_idx,\n        \"amount\": 0.0\n    })\n\nprint(f\"Total serialized documents: {len(corpus_documents):,} ({len(transaction_rows)} txs + {len(blocks_dict)} blocks)\")\n\n# Identify transaction types\ndelivery_rows = [\n    r for r in transaction_rows\n    if \"delivery\" in str(r[\"tx_type\"]).lower()\n]\n\npayment_rows = [\n    r for r in transaction_rows\n    if \"payment\" in str(r[\"tx_type\"]).lower()\n]\n\n# Build payment keys using the specified matching rule:\n# same block + delivery recipient = payment sender + exact amount\npayment_keys = {\n    (\n        int(r[\"block_index\"]),\n        str(r[\"tx_sender\"]),\n        round(float(r[\"tx_amount\"]), 6)\n    )\n    for r in payment_rows\n}\n\nunmatched_deliveries = []\n\nfor r in delivery_rows:\n    delivery_key = (\n        int(r[\"block_index\"]),\n        str(r[\"tx_recipient\"]),\n        round(float(r[\"tx_amount\"]), 6)\n    )\n\n    if delivery_key not in payment_keys:\n        unmatched_deliveries.append(r)\n\n# Create a dataset-level evidence document\nsummary_text = (\n    \"Smart Grid Dataset Summary:\\n\"\n    f\"Total transaction records: {len(transaction_rows)}\\n\"\n    f\"Energy delivery transactions: {len(delivery_rows)}\\n\"\n    f\"Energy payment transactions: {len(payment_rows)}\\n\"\n    f\"Unmatched delivery transactions: {len(unmatched_deliveries)}\\n\"\n    \"Matching rule for unmatched deliveries: \"\n    \"A delivery is considered matched if a payment exists in the same block, \"\n    \"with the delivery recipient equal to the payment sender, \"\n    \"and with the exact same transaction amount.\\n\"\n    \"Interpretation: An unmatched delivery means no corresponding payment \"\n    \"was found under this specified matching rule. \"\n    \"It does not, by itself, establish fraud or payment failure.\"\n)\n\ncorpus_documents.append(summary_text)\ncorpus_ids.append(\"summary-dataset-overview-v1\")\ncorpus_metadatas.append({\n    \"doc_type\": \"dataset_summary\",\n    \"tx_id\": \"\",\n    \"tx_type\": \"dataset_summary\",\n    \"sender\": \"\",\n    \"recipient\": \"\",\n    \"block_index\": -1,\n    \"amount\": 0.0\n})\n\nprint(\"Dataset summary added:\")\nprint(f\"Deliveries: {len(delivery_rows)}\")\nprint(f\"Payments: {len(payment_rows)}\")\nprint(f\"Unmatched deliveries: {len(unmatched_deliveries)}\")","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-24T14:18:47.341704Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-24T14:18:47.342077Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-24T14:18:47.429404Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-11-24T14:18:47.342053Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-24T14:18:47.428582Z"}},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","text":"Total serialized documents: 10,695 (10205 txs + 490 blocks)\nDataset summary added:\nDeliveries: 5193\nPayments: 5012\nUnmatched deliveries: 181\n","output_type":"stream"}],"execution_count":4},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"## 3. Store Vectors in ChromaDB\nWe create a persistent ChromaDB collection using HNSW indexing with cosine distance and `all-MiniLM-L6-v2` embeddings.\n","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"chroma_client = chromadb.PersistentClient(path=CHROMA_PATH)\nembed_fn = embedding_functions.SentenceTransformerEmbeddingFunction(\n    model_name=EMBEDDING_MODEL_NAME,\n    device=\"cuda\" if torch.cuda.is_available() else \"cpu\"\n)\n\nexisting = [c.name for c in chroma_client.list_collections()]\nif COLLECTION_NAME in existing:\n    collection = chroma_client.get_collection(COLLECTION_NAME, embedding_function=embed_fn)\n    print(f\"Found existing collection '{COLLECTION_NAME}' with {collection.count():,} items.\")\n    if collection.count() < len(corpus_documents):\n        chroma_client.delete_collection(COLLECTION_NAME)\n        collection = chroma_client.create_collection(\n            name=COLLECTION_NAME,\n            embedding_function=embed_fn,\n            metadata={\"hnsw:space\": \"cosine\"}\n        )\nelse:\n    collection = chroma_client.create_collection(\n        name=COLLECTION_NAME,\n        embedding_function=embed_fn,\n        metadata={\"hnsw:space\": \"cosine\"}\n    )\n\nif collection.count() == 0:\n    print(f\"Indexing {len(corpus_documents):,} documents into ChromaDB...\")\n    start_time = time.time()\n    batch_size = 500\n    for i in range(0, len(corpus_documents), batch_size):\n        end_idx = min(i + batch_size, len(corpus_documents))\n        collection.add(\n            ids=corpus_ids[i:end_idx],\n            documents=corpus_documents[i:end_idx],\n            metadatas=corpus_metadatas[i:end_idx]\n        )\n        if (i // batch_size) % 5 == 0 or end_idx == len(corpus_documents):\n            print(f\"  Indexed {end_idx:,} / {len(corpus_documents):,} ({((end_idx)/len(corpus_documents))*100:.1f}%)\")\n    print(f\"Indexing completed in {time.time() - start_time:.2f} s.\")\n\nprint(f\"Active collection count: {collection.count():,} documents.\")\n","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-24T14:18:47.430596Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-24T14:18:47.430975Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-24T14:19:37.063109Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-11-24T14:18:47.430941Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-24T14:19:37.062362Z"}},"outputs":[{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":"modules.json:   0%|          | 0.00/349 [00:00<?, ?B/s]","application/vnd.jupyter.widget-view+json":{"version_major":2,"version_minor":0,"model_id":"a816c4a079bf46879fa06439dd57f3d4"}},"metadata":{}},{"name":"stderr","text":"Warning: You are sending unauthenticated requests to the HF Hub. Please set a HF_TOKEN to enable higher rate limits and faster downloads.\n","output_type":"stream"},{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":"config_sentence_transformers.json:   0%|          | 0.00/116 [00:00<?, ?B/s]","application/vnd.jupyter.widget-view+json":{"version_major":2,"version_minor":0,"model_id":"70475d4d6dbc43c682f77776645b5601"}},"metadata":{}},{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":"README.md:   0%|          | 0.00/10.5k [00:00<?, ?B/s]","application/vnd.jupyter.widget-view+json":{"version_major":2,"version_minor":0,"model_id":"25f55e25af374aa09ac51608c2782396"}},"metadata":{}},{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":"sentence_bert_