s for Vector RAG:\n1. **Strengths (Single-Hop & Semantic Queries):** High retrieval precision and answer accuracy on single-hop lookups (S1, S2) and semantic/descriptive overviews (D1, D2) where the query text semantically matches document sentences.\n2. **Multi-Hop Blindspot:** On relational multi-hop queries (M1, M2), top-5 vector similarity retrieves the delivery transaction document, but completely fails to link the corresponding payment transaction in the same block, because separate flat documents lack explicit semantic cross-references.\n3. **Aggregation Trade-off (Chunk vs. Hierarchical Summary):**\n   - Under *standard flat-chunk Vector RAG*, global aggregations (A1, A2) fail because top-5 chunk retrieval can only observe 5 out of 10,205 transactions (coverage < 0.05%).\n   - Under *hierarchical/summary-enhanced Vector RAG* (with `summary-dataset-overview-v1`), Vector RAG can answer dataset-level questions if summary documents are indexed in advance.\n4. **Model Scaling (4B vs. 8B Ablation):** Scaling the generator from Qwen3-4B to Qwen3-8B improves SQuAD token F1 and structured JSON adherence, but does not overcome retrieval-stage omissions (retrieval bottleneck).\n5. **Hallucination & Refusal Safety:** On unanswerable queries (U1, U2), both models achieve 100% refusal accuracy by adhering to the strict schema instruction `{\"claims\": []}` when evidence is absent.\n","metadata":{}}]}